    one spatial-noise ray offset, deterministic arithmetic midpoints of quadratic shadow intervals,
    direct threshold termination and the four-frame reconstruction-coordinate phase cycle.
  The policy now excludes optical-mass sample placement, full-support accumulation prepasses,
    reused detail multipliers and separate residual-support/attenuation marches. Exact arbitrary-
    column optical depth remains an independent reference, not a hidden production integration pass.
    Native finite bounds and existing OIT outputs remain explicit adaptations with quality checks.
  Revised arithmetic receipts are artifacts/CloudRealtime/policy-revision/check-policy-math.ps1 and
    policy-math-results.json, separate from the frozen baseline evidence. Checks passed for eleven
    primary examples, ninety supported-control combinations, uniform spacing/weights, ten quadratic
    shadow intervals, five finite-exit examples, six legacy mappings and three nonfinite fallbacks.
    The ten shadow weights sum to 1500 world units; arithmetic midpoint positions are 7.5..1357.5.
    Default worst-case bounds are 192 secondary rays and 1920 secondary density evaluations per
    primary ray, and quarter-to-half reconstruction has four phases. These are specification checks;
    version precedence remains truth-table review, not runtime deserialization testing.
  A second consistency pass reconciled each candidate conflict against all task outcomes, policy
    definitions and acceptance sections. No reportable planning discrepancy remains. Later phases
    remain unchecked; finite-budget thin-feature quality, blue-noise assets, clean-break settings,
    runtime correctness, measured speed and changed-renderer appearance still require implementation
    and their stated qualification. Phase 1 covers the retained baseline and this revised specification.

